      "dom_id": "question-170877",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Suppose $v$ is directly proportional to $u.$ Given that $v=-12$ when $u=3$, find the value of $v$ when $u=5.${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Since $v$ varies directly with $u,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\nv=ku.\n$$\n\nWe are told that $v=-12$ when $u=3.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12 & =k\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{(-12)}{3} & =k \\\\ -4 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the direct variation equation is given by\n\n$$\nv=-4u.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the value of $u=5$ into this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =-4\\cdot 5=-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
